# A2A Nexus CODEOWNERS
#
# Review-routing for the public-readiness alpha repository. This does not move finalizer
# authority to workers, is not a stable public maintainer roster, and does not
# authorize releases, package publication, production deploys, repository
# visibility changes, secret movement, history rewrites, or force pushes.
#
# Routing only. `main` has require_code_owner_review=false, so these entries
# request review; they do not gate the merge. The merge gate is
# required_approving_review_count=1 plus the required status checks.
#
# First handle on each line is the PRIMARY reviewer; @seoseo-ai is the designated
# BACKUP so review does not degrade into self-approval or an unbounded wait when
# the primary is unavailable (#1507 bus-factor bullet; GOVERNANCE.md "Backup
# reviewer path"). The backup is listed on EVERY line on purpose: CODEOWNERS
# resolves by last-matching-pattern, so naming it only on `*` would leave every
# path listed below covered by a single reviewer — exactly the risk this is meant
# to remove.

* @jinon86 @seoseo-ai

# Public umbrella, contracts, fixtures, readiness gates, and coordination docs.
